The project is named **NoDeck** (NoDE DEck - deduplicated).
Repository: https://github.com/mprivoro/NoDeck

## Version 1.0
## 2026-08-25

Fork of [lxc-webpanel/LXC-Web-Panel](https://github.com/lxc-webpanel/LXC-Web-Panel) (archived 2020).
Maintained independently as NoDeck (formerly LXC-Web).

+ Python 3 support for the panel on current Ubuntu/LXC
+ Read modern LXC config keys (`lxc.net.0.*`, `lxc.uts.name`, `lxc.rootfs.path`) as well as the old 0.8/0.9 names
+ Allow duplicate keys in container configs (`lxc.include` and similar); Python 3 ConfigParser no longer crashes after login
+ Memory usage on cgroup v2 via `memory.current` (fallback to `memory.usage_in_bytes`)
+ Host distro from `/etc/os-release` (`platform.linux_distribution()` was removed in Python 3.8)
+ Wider layout: page uses the browser width instead of Bootstrap 2's 940px box (`static/css/lwp.css`)
+ `secret_key` is configurable in `lwp.conf` (`[session]`) instead of a hardcoded Flask secret
+ Serve jQuery 1.9.1 from `static/js/` (no Google CDN)
+ Autostart detection via `lxc.start.auto`

* Version check no longer contacts lxc-webpanel.github.io; About shows the local `version` file only
* Dropped html5shim and other third-party script URLs from templates
* About page and footer rebranded; MIT copyright for 2013 and 2026 kept in `LICENSE`
* README rewritten: clone, install, run, update, default URL and admin login
* Removed unused `static/css/bootstrap-select.min.css` (GitHub HTML dump) and `templates/includes/modals.html`
* Removed unused `/_check_version` route

## Version 0.2 beta
## 2013-04-30

Upstream LXC Web Panel.

+ Instant push memory and CPU options to cgroup values
+ Added partition option in the config file, you can choose which partition you want to monitor in the overview
+ If there is no container, the panel will display the modal "Create CT"
+ Added clone CT feature
+ Added "start at boot" button
+ Added support for multiple key/value (only for lxc.cgroup.devices.deny and lxc.cgroup.devices.allow) in container's config file (with ConfigParser)
+ Added support for templates option (Create CT)

* Now, in the sidebar, links are highlighted for containers edit pages
* Added modal to confirm the deletion of a user
  * Can't delete a user if he is the only one
  * Can't delete a admin user if there is no other admin user
* Splited modals files
* Now, simple users can't edit/create/destroy CTs and they can't reboot the host.
* Allowed '-' in rootfs path (thanks to mkobel)
* Changed regexp for hostname
* Fixed checkconfig if kernel headers are not installed
